      "text": "🌬 Locrian Finally Makes Sense | Minor ii–V–i on Harmonica\n🔥 Watch the full Locrian lesson with on-screen harmonica tabs on Patreon:\nhttps://patreon.com/konstantinreinfeld\nSave 20% with the annual Patreon membership.\n🎵 Locrian Harmonica Lesson – Minor ii–V–i\nIn this video, we explore the Locrian mode through one of its most useful musical applications: the minor ii–V–i progression.\nUnlike the other modes, Locrian doesn’t give us a very stable tonal home. Its tonic chord is diminished, so instead of simply sitting on the mode, we use it where it naturally appears in harmony.\nIn A minor:\nBm7♭5 → E7 → Am\nB Locrian fits perfectly over the Bm7♭5 chord and gives us a practical way to actually hear and use the mode in real music.\n👉 Watch the full lesson with tabs here:\nhttps://patreon.com/konstantinreinfeld\nChoose the annual membership to save 20%.\n//\n► Online harmonica lessons:\nlessons@konstantinreinfeld.com\n► Patreon:\nhttps://patreon.com/konstantinreinfeld\n► DIY Harmonica:\nhttps://a.co/d/23xZIip\n► Website:\nhttps://konstantinreinfeld.com\n► Instagram:\nhttps://instagram.com/konstantin_reinfeld\n//\n#harmonica #locrian #harmonicalesson #jazzharmonica #251progression #modalplaying #modalimprov…",
