          "text": "A small detail built into the JDR GM-0648 chromatic harmonica is its anti-squeal design in the upper register.\nThe upper register on a chromatic harmonica is usually more sensitive to embouchure, tongue position, and breath control, especially for players who are still getting used to the way a chromatic responds.\nThe GM-0648 uses built-in inserts in the upper register to help reduce unwanted reed squeal and make those notes easier to control.\nhttps://www.facebook.com/JDRmusik/posts/pfbid02yMd6MaF9QuwkvhZ5mDf6WeRuMs8ZU1axQ8NVBE25NMDsqK76LAf4GbCy4mpUVgLrl",
