          "text": "Classic riffing: „Black Night“ on the PentaHarp 🕶️\nSometimes you just need a solid rock line. In this quick video, @chris_kramer_harmonica_player breaks down the iconic intro from „Black Night.“\n⚡ Why it fits the PentaHarp so well:\nHard rock is built on the minor pentatonic scale. Because the PentaHarp lays out these exact notes directly, you don’t have to fight through awkward breath jumps—you can just focus on laying down that tone with great timing.\nThe tabs are displayed on screen—grab your harp and play along.\n👉 Check out Chris’ full masterclass series on @HohnerMusic (YouTube), neatly organized across 7 languages. And don’t forget to follow @ChrisKramerChannel for more breakdowns.",
