          "text": "I’ve played the diatonic harmonica for most of my life, and I’m still looking for ways to push it somewhere it hasn’t been before.\n“Niccolò’s Notion” came from my longtime fascination with Paganini’s Moto Perpetuo. I wanted to find out whether that same idea of relentless, continuous motion could live on a 10-hole harmonica.\nThis piece was my answer. Here’s your first taste of the studio recording.\nAugust 28. 🔥The lead single from my new solo album, Heavy World.\n#harmonica #harmonicaplayer #howardlevy #newmusiccomingsoon #neverbefore",
